Adds ~50 LOC to make Claude Code's --effort {low,medium,high,xhigh} flag
flow end-to-end through copilot-api when the upstream is Copilot
Enterprise. Without this patch, Claude Code emits
thinking: {type: "enabled", budget_tokens: N} in /v1/messages, copilot-api
forwards as-is, and Copilot's Vertex-backed Anthropic endpoint silently
drops the field — so every Claude Code session on Copilot loses its
effort tier silently.

Translation maps budget_tokens to a tier name and clamps per-model based
on the live catalog at /models (queried on api.enterprise.githubcopilot.com
on 2026-05-29):
  - low      → budget < 4096
  - medium   → 4096-15999
  - high     → 16000-49999
  - xhigh    → >= 50000
Per-model allowed sets prevent upstream HTTP 400 by silently degrading
unsupported tiers. Only claude-opus-4.7-1m-internal (Microsoft-internal
variant) currently accepts xhigh on Copilot Enterprise; plain 4.7 and 4.8
are catalog-restricted to ["medium"] only.

See PATCH_NOTES.md for the full investigation (4 layers of evidence),
deployment topology, verification probes, revert path, and the maintenance
plan for when claude-opus-4.8-internal eventually ships.

